Run records of what the port does that the Go compiler does not, each a
port-only check, which stands for no Go test and has an entry in tackc's
porttest/testdata/divergences.txtar; see tools/corpus/runs.tck for the
format. A release rewrites every stdout "tack devel\n" line of
this archive, in the copy of the tree it builds from, with its version, as
it rewrites driver/version.tck (see tools/release/stamp.sh), so the
release's compiler is held to its own version.
-- version-flag-one-dash/record --
port-only tack -version, the one-dash spelling every flag has (decided 2026-11-21)
dir examples/hello
cwd empty
invoke "-version"
exit 0
stdout "tack devel\n"
stderr ""
-- version-ignores-the-rest/record --
port-only tack --version needs nothing else from the command line, and wins over --backends (decided 2026-11-21)
dir examples/hello
cwd empty
invoke "--backends"
invoke "--version"
invoke "--check"
invoke "missing.tck"
invoke "another.tck"
exit 0
stdout "tack devel\n"
stderr ""
-- version-prints-the-version/record --
port-only tack --version, which the Go compiler does not have (decided 2026-11-21)
dir examples/hello
cwd empty
invoke "--version"
exit 0
stdout "tack devel\n"
stderr ""
